{"case": "fit_smile_with_humps", "fit": {"source": "Market quotes", "carry": 0.04, "calendar_violations": 0, "butterfly_violations": 0, "quoted_points": 205, "notes": ["The SVI smile is more than 1 vol point (RMSE) from the quotes at maturities 2y, where no arbitrage-free smile can follow them: at those vols a put costs less than one at a lower strike, or a call more than one at a lower strike. Check those quotes and the maturity unit (days to expiry read as years give smiles this steep). The Smiles chart shows how far the fit is from each quote.", "The SVI smile is more than 1 vol point (RMSE) from the quotes at maturities 0.0822y, 0.249y, 0.499y, 1y: the quotes there are noisy, or their smile has a shape a single SVI curve cannot follow (an SVI smile has one trough and no humps). The Smiles chart shows how far the fit is from each quote.", "The quotes have static arbitrage that the fitted surface smooths out: at maturities 0.249y, 0.499y, 1y a butterfly of neighbouring strikes costs less than nothing (a negative risk-neutral density) even if each quote is 0.5 vol point off, e.g. 87.5/90/92.5 at 0.249y. The checks also allow the unknown price behind each quoted implied vol to be off by 0.01% of the forward or 0.005 (at most 1% of the strike spacing), whichever is more. At maturities 0.249y the arbitrage is small enough that rounding the prices behind the quoted vols to 0.05 ticks could cause it, so it may not be in the market. The arbitrage counts above describe the fitted surface, not the quotes, so check these quotes."], "maturities": [0.0821917808, 0.2493150685, 0.498630137, 1.0, 2.0], "moneyness": {"shape": [41], "nan": 0, "sum": 42.02500000000012, "sha256": "d505e8ab8c3ce8dae87def2f6329f2aceafc9bd814b0b9723c91bee95e55f68f"}, "implied_vol": {"shape": [5, 41], "nan": 0, "sum": 52.51228926919415, "sha256": "51b6da950b3bd053ef11ffc80da039a977d5b7ea8018ebc2aba4f9d9f31e009d"}, "local_vol": {"shape": [5, 41], "nan": 0, "sum": 53.234827316200864, "sha256": "24d7b8166c